1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:01,210
One man.

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,330
One red button.

3
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:06,330
And one decision
that saved the world.

4
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:10,860
September twenty-sixth,
nineteen eighty-three.

5
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:12,970
A secret bunker near Moscow.

6
00:00:13,850 --> 00:00:15,940
Lieutenant Colonel
Stanislav Petrov is on

7
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:18,362
night duty, watching
the sky for American

8
00:00:18,382 --> 00:00:19,370
missiles.

9
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:21,410
The world was on edge.

10
00:00:21,590 --> 00:00:22,770
Three weeks earlier,

11
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:24,260
the Soviet Union
had shot down a

12
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:25,530
passenger plane.

13
00:00:25,830 --> 00:00:27,210
Everyone expected war.

14
00:00:28,270 --> 00:00:29,280
Just after midnight,

15
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:30,970
the alarm screamed.

16
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:32,043
The computer said:

17
00:00:32,063 --> 00:00:34,527
one missile, launched
from America.

18
00:00:34,547 --> 00:00:35,723
Then another.

19
00:00:35,743 --> 00:00:36,815
And another.

20
00:00:36,835 --> 00:00:39,453
Five missiles, inbound.

21
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:40,423
The screen read:

22
00:00:40,443 --> 00:00:41,212
Launch.

23
00:00:41,232 --> 00:00:42,893
Confidence:

24
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:44,013
high.

25
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:45,613
The orders were clear.

26
00:00:45,730 --> 00:00:48,031
Report it, and Soviet
leaders would strike

27
00:00:48,051 --> 00:00:50,013
back with
everything they had.

28
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:51,343
Petrov had minutes.

29
00:00:51,363 --> 00:00:53,453
But something felt wrong.

30
00:00:54,043 --> 00:00:55,471
Why would America
start a war with

31
00:00:55,491 --> 00:00:56,943
only five missiles?

32
00:00:56,963 --> 00:00:59,023
And the ground
radar saw nothing.

33
00:00:59,043 --> 00:01:00,143
No proof.

34
00:01:00,163 --> 00:01:01,343
Just instinct.

35
00:01:01,363 --> 00:01:03,310
He picked up the phone...

36
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:04,093
and said:

37
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:05,135
False alarm.

38
00:01:05,155 --> 00:01:06,973
Then he waited.

39
00:01:07,470 --> 00:01:08,550
If he was wrong,

40
00:01:08,570 --> 00:01:10,013
cities would burn.

41
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:11,613
Minutes crawled by.

42
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:13,130
No explosions.

43
00:01:13,150 --> 00:01:14,533
No fire.

44
00:01:14,870 --> 00:01:16,676
The satellites had
mistaken sunlight,

45
00:01:16,696 --> 00:01:18,163
glinting off high clouds,

46
00:01:18,183 --> 00:01:19,373
for missiles.

47
00:01:20,190 --> 00:01:21,567
Petrov was never
made a hero at

48
00:01:21,587 --> 00:01:22,143
home.

49
00:01:22,163 --> 00:01:24,490
He died in two
thousand seventeen,

50
00:01:24,510 --> 00:01:27,053
in a quiet apartment
outside Moscow.

51
00:01:27,510 --> 00:01:29,743
But because one man
doubted a machine,

52
00:01:29,763 --> 00:01:31,733
we are all still here.

53
00:01:32,419 --> 00:01:34,333
Sometimes the
bravest thing...

54
00:01:34,370 --> 00:01:35,853
is not pressing the button.
